@NAME@
======

This folder holds an AI that learned to play. You don't need the Vyrn app to run it.

To run it
---------
1. You need Python 3.10 or newer.
2. Install the small helper it plays with (once). Open a terminal in this folder and type:

       pip install @WHEEL@

   If pip tells you the system is "externally managed", make a private Python first:

       python3 -m venv venv
       venv/bin/pip install @WHEEL@
       venv/bin/python play.py

3. Start it:

       python3 play.py

   It prints how many points it gets each round. Press Ctrl+C to stop.

Handy extras
------------
   python3 play.py --rounds 20      play 20 rounds, then stop
   python3 play.py --speed 0        a game that runs inside the computer: go as fast as possible
   python3 play.py --view           show a small window with what the AI sees
   python3 play.py --help           everything else

Games on your screen
--------------------
If the AI plays a real game with the keyboard, it only tells you which keys it would press. To let it press them
for real, add --allow-keys. You get 3 seconds to click on your game window, and the AI only presses keys while that
window is in front. Hands off the keyboard while it plays.

What is in this folder
----------------------
   brain.vrl      what the AI learned
   play.py        starts it
   *.py, vyrn.json   the scripts and settings it was taught with (open them in a text editor to see how it works)

Made with Vyrn @VERSION@.
